+---
+id: task-002-monthly-order-export-csv
+type: task
+title: "Monthly order export CSV"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Goal
+
+The accountant loads a monthly export of the orders into her spreadsheet. The first export is due at the end of October 2026.
+
+## Requirements
+
+- The order book offers `exportMonth(month)`, where `month` is `YYYY-MM`.
+- It returns CSV text: a header line, then one line per order placed in that month (its `date` starts with `YYYY-MM`), in order number order.
+- Columns, in this order: `order` (the order number), `date` (as the order stores it), `customer` (the customer's name), `total` (what the customer pays, `totalCents` in euros with two decimals, e.g. `12.50`).
+- The export carries no customer email address or phone number (rework after Dana Okafor's rejection).
+- A value containing a comma, a quote or a line break is quoted as CSV usually is (quotes doubled).
+- A month with no orders gives the header line alone.
+- A malformed `month` (not `YYYY-MM` with a month 01-12) is refused with an `invalid` error.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+- Header and rows are checked on a worked example, including a name with a comma and a quote, and the `total` formatting; the header has no email or phone column.
+- Orders from other months are left out; an empty month gives the header only.
+- A malformed month is refused.
+- Documented in the public API and in `CHANGELOG.md` under an unreleased heading (no version bump before approval).
